# Change: Am-Fmaj7 and C-F (repertoire plan: st-change-am-fmaj7-c-f). An original chord-change
# study. Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord held for two bars
# (one strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half (home Am): Am (x02210), fingered 2 on string 4, 3 on string 3, 1 on
# string 2, with Fmaj7 (xx3210): finger 1 stays on string 2 fret 1 (C), finger 3 moves to string 4
# fret 3 (F) and finger 2 to string 3 fret 2 (A). Second half (home C): C (x32010) with the small
# F (xx3211): fingers 3 and 2 move one string toward string 1 and finger 1 flattens across strings
# 2 and 1 at fret 1, a two-string barre and the first step toward the full F. Strum strings 4 to 1
# for both F shapes. Keep the metronome on: the new chord lands on the beat even if the strum
# before it catches open strings. The teacher plays an original tune that lands on a note of the
# new chord at every change (Fmaj7 is Am with F underneath: they share A, C and E); only in the
# second bar of a held chord does it lean on the note above and fall to it (D to C over Am, F to
# E over C), a suspension you can hear resolve.
title: Change: Am-Fmaj7 and C-F
id: st-change-am-fmaj7-c-f
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: chord changes, fmaj7, small f, two-string barre, metronome
